{"G1018":{"id":"G1018","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1018","disambiguated_id":"G1018 =","unique_id":"G1018","headword":"βραβεύω","transliteration":"brabeuō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to rule","definition_en":"βραβεύω \n (βραβεύς, an umpire), [in LXX: Wis.10:12 * ;] \n __(a) prop., to act as umpire; hence, \n __(b) generally, to arbitrate, decide (Isocr., Dem.; Lft., Col., l.with; MM, see word): Col.3:15; \n __(with) in some late writers, to direct, rule, control (so in Col., l.with, accusative to Thayer, see word, Meyer, in l.), (cf. κατα-βραβεύω).\n† (AS)","source_line":1140}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"governe","count":1}]},"G1059":{"id":"G1059","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1059","disambiguated_id":"G1059 =","unique_id":"G1059","headword":"Γαμαλιήλ","transliteration":"Gamaliēl","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Gamaliel","definition_en":"Γαμαλιήλ, ὁ (Heb. גַּמְלִיאֵל), \n Gamaliel the elder, a Pharisee and Doctor of the Law: Act.5:34 22:3.†\n (AS)","source_line":1185}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Gamaliel","count":2}]},"G1344":{"id":"G1344","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1344","disambiguated_id":"G1344 =","unique_id":"G1344","headword":"δικαιόω","transliteration":"dikaioō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to justify","definition_en":"δικαιόω, -ῶ\n (δίκαιος), [in LXX chiefly for צָדַק pi., hi., (1) as Eze.16:51, Jer.3:11 (cf. NT usage); (2) as Deu.25:1; Exo.23:7, Isa.50:8 ;] \n__1. in cl., \n __(a) with accusative of thing(s), to deem right; \n __(b) with accusative of person(s), to do one justice; pass., δικαιοῦσθαι, to be treated rightly, opposite to ἀδικεῖσθαι. \n __2. In NT, as in LXX, and as usual with verbs in -όω from adjectives of moral meaning; \n __(1) to show to be righteous: Mat.11:19, Luk.7:35, Rom.3:4\" (LXX), 1Ti.3:16; \n __(2) to declare, pronounce righteous: Luk.7:29 10:29 16:15 18:14, Rom.2:13 3:24, 26 3:28 4:5 8:30, 33, Tit.3:7; before ἀπό, Mat.11:19, Luk.7:35, Act.13:39, Rom.6:7; ἐκ πίστεως, Rom.3:30 5:1, Gal.2:16 3:8, 24; ἐξ ἔργων, Rom.3:20 (LXX) Rom.4:2, Gal.2:16, Jas.2:21, 24-25; ἐκ τ. λόγων, Mat.12:37; διὰ τ. πίστεως, Rom.3:30; with dative, Rom.3:24, 28, Tit.3:7; before ἐν, Act.13:39, Rom.3:4 5:9, 1Co.4:4 6:11, Gal.2:17 3:11 5:4, 1Ti.3:16 (see Cremer, 193, 693; DB, ii, 826 ff.).†\n (AS)","source_line":1476}],"occurrence_count":39,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"justificado","count":12},{"gloss":"justificados","count":4},{"gloss":"mas","count":2},{"gloss":"ser-justificados","count":2},{"gloss":"justificou","count":2},{"gloss":"sejamos-justificados","count":2},{"gloss":"justificaram","count":1},{"gloss":"justificar","count":1},{"gloss":"justificais","count":1},{"gloss":"justificador","count":1},{"gloss":"justificará","count":1},{"gloss":"justo","count":1},{"gloss":"absolvido","count":1},{"gloss":"justifica","count":1},{"gloss":"fostes-justificados","count":1},{"gloss":"é-justificado","count":1},{"gloss":"será-justificada","count":1},{"gloss":"justificaria","count":1},{"gloss":"quereis","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-sido-justificados","count":1},{"gloss":"quando","count":1}]},"G1656":{"id":"G1656","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1656","disambiguated_id":"G1656 =","unique_id":"G1656","headword":"ἔλεος","transliteration":"eleos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"mercy","definition_en":"ἔλεος, -ους, τό\n (cl. -ου, ὁ, and so Rec., Mat.9:13 12:7 23:23, Tit.3:5, Heb.4:16; on the Hellenistic form τό ἔ., see WH, App., 158; M, Pr., 60; Mayser, 277; Kühner, i, 515), [in LXX chiefly for חֶסֶד ;] \nmercy, pity, compassion; \n __1. of men: Mat.9:13 (LXX) Mat.12:7 23:23; ποιεῖν ἔ. (and id. before μετά, with genitive; cf. Heb. עִם חֶסֶד עָשָׂה, Gen.21:23, al.), Luk.10:37, Jas.2:13 3:17. \n __2. Of God: Luk.1:50, 54 1:58, Rom.15:9, Eph.2:4, 2Ti.1:16 1:18, Tit.3:5, Heb.4:16, 1Pe.1:3; esp. in benedictions, Gal.6:16, 1Ti.1:2, 2Ti.1:2, 2Jn.3, Ju 2; σκευὴ ἐλέους, Rom.9:23; σπλάγχνα ἐλέους, Luk.1:78; ποιεῖν ἔ. (see supr.), Luk.1:72; τ. ὑμετέρῳ ἐλέει, Rom.11:31. \n __3. Of Christ: Ju 21.†\n SYN.: οἰκτιρμός (see: ἐλεέω) (AS)","source_line":1796}],"occurrence_count":27,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"misericórdia","count":27}]},"G1669":{"id":"G1669","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1669","disambiguated_id":"G1669 =","unique_id":"G1669","headword":"ἑλκόω","transliteration":"helkoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to have/cause sores","definition_en":"ἑλκόω, -ῶ \n __1. to wound. \n __2. to ulcerate; pass., to suffer from sores: pf. ptcp., εἱλκωμίνος (Rec. ἡλκ-), EV, full of sores, Luk.16:20.†\n (AS)","source_line":1810}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"coberto-de-úlceras","count":1}]},"G1990":{"id":"G1990","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1990","disambiguated_id":"G1990 =","unique_id":"G1990","headword":"ἐπιστήμων","transliteration":"epistēmōn","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"knowing","definition_en":"ἐπιστήμων, -ον, genitive, -ονoς\n (ἐπίσταμαι) [in LXX: Deu.1:13 4:6, Isa.5:21 (בִּין ni.), I Est.8:44, Sir.10:25 21:15, etc. ;] \nknowing, skilled: Jas.3:13.†\n (AS)","source_line":2131}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"inteligente","count":1}]},"G2507":{"id":"G2507","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2507","disambiguated_id":"G2507 =","unique_id":"G2507","headword":"καθαιρέω","transliteration":"kathaireō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to take down","definition_en":"καθ-αιρέω, -ῶ \n [in LXX for נָתַץ, פָּרַץ, יָרַד, etc. ;] \n__1. to take down: with accusative of person(s) (the technical term for removal after crucifixion, Field, Notes, 44), Mrk.15:36, 46, Luk.23:53, Act.13:29. \n __2. to put down by force, pull down, destroy: ἀποθήκας, Luk.12:18 (opposite to οἰκοδομεῖν); δυνάστας, Luk.1:52; ἔθνη, Act.13:19; pass., Act.19:27 (diminished, Field, Notes, 129 f.); figuratively, to refute: λογισμούς, 2Co.10:5.†\n (AS)","sourc